      en: "The Nosy Be Lighthouse, situated at the extreme southern point of the island near the crater lakes of Mont Passot, is a striking maritime landmark. Built to ensure the safe navigation of ships passing through the busy Mozambique Channel and entering the deep-water harbor of Hell-Ville, the tall, slender white tower offers panoramic views of the surrounding archipelago, including Nosy Komba and Nosy Tanikely. Constructed during the colonial era, the lighthouse remains an operational navigational aid. The site is a popular destination for tourists, particularly at sunset, offering a vantage point over the lush, volcanic topography of the 'Perfume Island' and the vast expanse of the Indian Ocean. Geografi K6 — maritime navigation and island topography."
