      en: "The Arcades of Independence Avenue (Avenue de l'Indépendance) form the most iconic urban landmark in Antananarivo. This massive, wide boulevard stretches through the lower city (Analakely) and is flanked on both sides by long, continuous, two-story white buildings featuring distinct arched colonnades on the ground floor. Built by the French in the 1930s, the arcades were designed to house commercial shops while providing pedestrians with shade and protection from the heavy highland rains. Today, the avenue terminates at the historic Gare Soarano and is the bustling heart of the capital's street commerce, hosting everything from high-end boutiques to chaotic street vendors. Geografi K7 — urban planning and commercial boulevards."
