      en: "The Katedraly Saint-Laurent de Faravohitra is a massive Catholic cathedral perched prominently on the Faravohitra hill, visible from almost anywhere in Antananarivo. Built between 1899 and 1930, the cathedral is a stunning example of Romanesque-Byzantine architecture, constructed entirely of precisely cut, exposed red clay bricks that blend perfectly with the surrounding Trano Gasy highland houses. The cathedral features a massive central dome and tall twin towers, though one tower remained unfinished for decades. Its elevated position offers breathtaking panoramic views of the city. The building serves as a spiritual anchor for the upper city and is a masterpiece of local Malagasy masonry and brickwork. Geografi K7 — religious landmarks and traditional brickwork."
