      en: "The Pirate Cemetery on Île Sainte-Marie (Nosy Boraha) is a famous, evocative landmark representing the golden age of Indian Ocean piracy. Situated on a small, lush hill overlooking the Baie des Forbans (Pirates' Bay), the site contains roughly 30 dark, weathered tombstones dating back to the 17th and 18th centuries. The graves belong to notorious pirates, privateers, and smugglers who used the island's hidden coves to launch attacks on treasure ships returning from the East Indies. Several gravestones still bear the faint, chilling engravings of a skull and crossbones. Accessible only by a narrow, muddy path that floods at high tide, the cemetery is a haunting monument to the island's lawless, legendary past. Geschichte K7 — maritime piracy and historical gravesites."
